#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101604} :activity/id #uuid "752a2e8d-dfc4-5210-8dfe-31f383092e9e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050166 :topic/id #uuid "3342477c-42d1-5dd5-8ebd-975b2a6a85a5" :topic/math-academy-id 1204} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101604 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186102004 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given the graph of the function $f(x),$ as shown below. The function has critical points at $x=-1,$ $x=2,$ and an inflection point at $x=0.5.$\nHow can we sketch the graph of the derivative $f'(x)?$\n\n![](images/b3/b3fcc7a08d2a083567cc2de62c9bb0c6e9516552c8a2f08d2e814604f5ec84f8.png)\n\nNotice the following:\n\n- At the stationary points, where the tangent line to $y=f(x)$ is parallel to the $x$-axis, we have $f'(x)=0.$\n\n- When $f(x)$ is increasing, we have $f'(x) > 0.$\n\n- When $f(x)$ is decreasing, we have $f'(x) < 0.$\n\nWe can now summarize the information from the graph in the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty,-1)$ | $-1$ | $(-1,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f$ | $\\nearrow$ | $\\textrm{max}$ | $\\searrow$ | $\\textrm{min}$ | $\\nearrow$ |\n| $f'$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n\nUsing this information, we can identify the regions where $f'(x)$ should cross the $x$-axis. According to the table, these are points $(-1,0)$ and $(2,0)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/e9/e98d21084e06d2a28509b0b68f449c5f42959ee1adad9b3dbf912885968a3b33.png)\n\nAdditionally, we are told that the function has an inflection point at $x = 0.5.$ So $f''(0.5)=0$ and the tangent to the graph of $y=f'(x)$ must be parallel to the $x$-axis.\n\nWe don't know the exact value of $f'(0.5)$ but from the graph of $y=f(x),$ we can conclude that at $x = 0.5$ the slope is negative. Therefore, we get a point below the $x$-axis:\n\n![](images/59/5994a9139fbd1c530692a2fb40b2fb1b4b7bd0b34b2bf7ff7194390542748977.png)\n\nFinally, connecting up the parts of the graph above, we get an approximate sketch of $f'(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/f2/f21fca7744d7196e457f0a9d4511f644a3cf1e8c61018c152fc74ea7f6999f3e.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "732e85fe-aec5-51f6-806c-68e476077346" :tutorial/math-academy-id 641 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "beaa6f10-10cb-5300-9425-d5fce50a2dec" :step/math-academy-id 1224 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101771}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101605 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100825 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100638 :question/id #uuid "c6ce8503-265f-5a02-93f4-ad99390c2734" :question/math-academy-id "e-333"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3433cbc0-fe8c-5b67-a888-4df13b4b68c3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101301} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101306} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505759} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505810} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505811} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505827}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Derivative of a Smooth Function"} :step/id #uuid "1ebc76df-237a-5efb-96f2-b3585e2b318b" :step/math-academy-id 1225 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101772}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101606 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100826 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100639 :question/id #uuid "68f7ad36-cab7-5ffe-99d9-e720bbf7971a" :question/math-academy-id "e-334"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2ef7a61-79b9-5464-ac2a-3afb7dddd1c2" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101303} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101305} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503654} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505730} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505750} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505764} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505775} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505829}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Second Derivative of a Function"} :step/id #uuid "fe6a977a-c724-5c50-9d38-b0a7dc613ae3" :step/math-academy-id 1229} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101771 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100929 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/r